"alternate_generic_names","proposed_value":"","rationale":"No separate alternate generic name requiring row de-duplication was identified. Peganone belongs in trade_names/pubmed_search_aliases, not alternate_generic_names.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://api.fda.gov/drug/drugsfda.json?search=products.active_ingredients.name:%22ETHOTOIN%22&limit=5","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2010/010841s022lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"No - discontinued FDA Orange Book product","field":"available_in_us","proposed_value":"No - discontinued FDA/openFDA Drugs@FDA product","rationale":"FDA/openFDA Drugs@FDA lists Peganone oral tablet products as Discontinued.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://api.fda.gov/drug/drugsfda.json?search=products.active_ingredients.name:%22ETHOTOIN%22&limit=5"]},{"current_value":"Historical/unspecified epilepsy (specific FDA-labeled seizure category not available from Orange Book listing)","field":"epilepsy_type","proposed_value":"Tonic-clonic (grand mal) and complex partial (psychomotor) seizures","rationale":"FDA Peganone labeling states these labeled seizure indications; the row should not remain unspecified.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2010/010841s022lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Historical oral tablet (not marketed in U.S.)","field":"formulations_available","proposed_value":"Historical oral tablets: Peganone 250 mg in FDA label; FDA/openFDA Drugs@FDA lists discontinued Peganone oral tablet products at 250 mg and 500 mg.","rationale":"The formulation is oral tablet, but FDA sources support specific historical strengths and discontinued status.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2010/010841s022lbl.pdf","https://api.fda.gov/drug/drugsfda.json?search=products.active_ingredients.name:%22ETHOTOIN%22&limit=5"]},{"current_value":"N/A - no current FDA/DailyMed label located and FDA Orange Book product listing does not provide half-life.","field":"half_life_range","proposed_value":"3-9 hours at plasma concentrations below about 8 mcg/mL; FDA label also notes a reported half-life of 6-9 hours with 4-6 hour dosing intervals.","rationale":"FDA Peganone labeling provides half-life information; the no-label rationale is contradicted by FDA labeling.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2010/010841s022lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"N/A - no current FDA/DailyMed label located and FDA Orange Book product listing does not provide metabolism information.","field":"major_organ_for_metabolism","proposed_value":"Liver; FDA label states ethotoin is apparently biotransformed by the liver.","rationale":"FDA labeling supports hepatic metabolism/biotransformation.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2010/010841s022lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"N/A - no current FDA/DailyMed label located; FDA Orange Book confirms historical U.S. product approval/listing but does not provide mechanism of action.","field":"mechanism_of_action","proposed_value":"Hydantoin antiepileptic; mechanism probably similar to phenytoin: stabilizes rather than raises seizure threshold and prevents spread of seizure activity.","rationale":"FDA Peganone labeling provides a limited, phenytoin-like mechanism statement.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2010/010841s022lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Limited","field":"mechanism_confidence","proposed_value":"Limited","rationale":"The FDA label uses probabilistic mechanism wording, so limited confidence is appropriate.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2010/010841s022lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"FDA Orange Book products file","field":"mechanism_source","proposed_value":"FDA Peganone (ethotoin) labeling (accessdata.fda.gov; NDA010841/S-022)","rationale":"The Orange Book/Drugs@FDA product listing supports product status, not mechanism. The mechanism statement is supported by FDA labeling.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2010/010841s022lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Historical/limited","field":"mechanism_source_tier","proposed_value":"FDA labeling","rationale":"The mechanism source should be the FDA label, not the Orange Book product listing.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2010/010841s022lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"N/A - no current FDA/DailyMed label located and FDA Orange Book product listing does not describe enzyme induction or inhibition.","field":"enzyme_inducing_or_inhibiting","proposed_value":"Limited/unknown: FDA label does not document ethotoin enzyme induction/inhibition; it notes saturable metabolism and cautions that a phenytoin-like coumarin anticoagulant interaction may occur without documentation.","rationale":"FDA labeling exists and includes metabolism/drug-interaction discussion, but it does not establish a clear enzyme induction/inhibition classification.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2010/010841s022lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"N/A - no current FDA/DailyMed label located and FDA Orange Book product listing does not provide a maximum approved daily dose.","field":"maximum_approved_daily_dose","proposed_value":"3 g/day (upper end of usual adult maintenance dose; label does not state a separate maximum)","rationale":"FDA labeling gives usual adult maintenance dosing of 2 to 3 g daily.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2010/010841s022lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"N/A - no current FDA/DailyMed label located and FDA Orange Book product listing does not provide a minimum effective dose.","field":"minimum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"Adults: 2 g/day; FDA label states less than 2 g/day has been ineffective in most adults.","rationale":"FDA labeling provides an adult lower effective threshold statement.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2010/010841s022lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"N/A - no current FDA/DailyMed label located and FDA Orange Book product listing does not provide dosing.","field":"typical_doses_per_day","proposed_value":"4 to 6 divided doses daily, after food.","rationale":"FDA Peganone labeling specifies administration in 4 to 6 divided daily doses after food.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2010/010841s022lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"N/A 0%: no current FDA/DailyMed label identified; FDA Orange Book product listing does not provide adverse-event percentages.","field":"adverse_symptoms_percentages","proposed_value":"N/A: FDA Peganone label lists adverse reactions qualitatively and does not provide adverse-event incidence percentages.","rationale":"FDA labeling exists and lists adverse reactions without percentages; the Orange Book/product listing does not provide AE incidence data.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2010/010841s022lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"N/A - no current FDA/DailyMed label located and FDA Orange Book product listing does not describe QT effect.","field":"qt_interval_effect","proposed_value":"N/A - FDA Peganone label does not describe a QT-interval effect.","rationale":"The QT fact remains limited/unknown, but the source rationale should use FDA labeling rather than no-label wording.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2010/010841s022lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Approved Prior to Jan 1, 1982 (FDA Orange Book)","field":"year_fda_cleared","proposed_value":"1957 (FDA/openFDA Drugs@FDA original approval Apr 22, 1957; Orange Book may display Approved prior to Jan 1, 1982)","rationale":"The current value is consistent with pre-1982 Orange Book display, but FDA/openFDA Drugs@FDA provides the exact original approval date.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://api.fda.gov/drug/drugsfda.json?search=products.active_ingredients.name:%22ETHOTOIN%22&limit=5","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/appletter/2010/010841s022ltr.pdf"]},{"current_value":"FDA Orange Book products file; FDA/DailyMed labeling","field":"evidence_sources","proposed_value":"FDA/openFDA Drugs@FDA; FDA Peganone labeling (accessdata.fda.gov); PubMed","rationale":"DailyMed should not be used for boxed-warning verification, and Orange Book/product files do not support mechanism, dosing, half-life, metabolism, or adverse-reaction details. FDA label and PubMed sources should be named.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://api.fda.gov/drug/drugsfda.json?search=products.active_ingredients.name:%22ETHOTOIN%22&limit=5","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2010/010841s022lbl.pdf","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/?term=%28ethotoin%5BTitle%2FAbstract%5D+OR+Peganone%5BTitle%2FAbstract%5D%29+AND+%28randomized+OR+randomised+OR+placebo+OR+trial%29"]},{"current_value":"Historical/unspecified epilepsy","field":"filter_epilepsy_type","proposed_value":"Tonic-clonic and complex partial seizures","r